# Cross-BUILD A/B: capture one world state at mode 0 only.
#
# PREREQUISITE: a THROWAWAY clone of an explored save, passed as --var WORLD=<name>.
# See lightmode-world.vv for the clone command and why it must be a save you can lose.
#
# Deliberately minimal, and that is the point: this runs against OLD binaries that lack the
# newer diagnostics. At 9ff6719e31 and d438dc71e0 the F7 handler does not log the mode it
# lands on (that arrived in 368122c9f0) and debug view 16 does not exist (the modulo was 16,
# so the cycle never reached it). A scenario using `waitlog "lighting debug mode N"` would
# stall its whole timeout and abort AFTER the build had already been paid for. So: no F7,
# no debug views, mode 0 only.
#
# Mode 0 is the entire claim anyway. This answers the one question left open by
# plans/lighting-composition-pipeline.md Phase 1: is the wire-format change -- carrying
# light_mode to the shader WITHOUT reading it -- actually inert at the pixel level? Capture
# `world.png` from a build at 9ff6719e31 and from one at d438dc71e0, then require the
# cross-build difference to sit at or below each run's own paired same-state null.
#
# The window resizes shortly after the world loads (measured 1920x1080, then 2560x1440 1.5 s
# later), so a warm-up capture and a second settle come first: a size change between the two
# measured shots aborts the run.
launch --dont-debugmsg --world ${WORLD}
waitlog "opened document .*sidebar_hud.rml" timeout=300000
focus
settle timeout=25000
shot warmup avg=4
wait 6000
settle timeout=15000

# Conservative rect, well inside the map viewport: the HUD sidebar and the message bar are
# drawn on is_lit=false segments and are not part of the lighting composite at all.
rect play 0.25,0.12,0.55,0.80

shot world avg=12
wait 1500
shot world_again avg=12
diff world world_again as=same_state in=play
stats world in=play

log
stop
